rounds.answer1:
The standard procedure when a user cannot recall their password is:  
(1) Click **“Forgot Password”** on the login page;  
(2) Enter the associated email address or username;  
(3) Receive a **time-limited, one-time password (OTP)** or **reset link** via secure channel (e.g., email, SMS);  
(4) Verify identity through **multi-factor authentication (MFA)** if enabled;  
(5) Create a **new, strong password**;  
(6) Update the password in all devices and password manager.  

The process must be secure, encrypted, and logged. No password is ever revealed by the service. If the recovery method is compromised (e.g., email hacked), MFA and account recovery policies (e.g., security questions, backup codes) provide fallbacks. Unauthorized access attempts are blocked. This procedure ensures accountability, privacy, and compliance with GDPR, FCRA, and security best practices.

