rounds.answer1:
The secure reinitialization of credentials follows this operational sequence:  
(1) **User initiates reset** via “Forgot Password” with pre-registered email;  
(2) **System generates a time-bound, cryptographically signed token** (e.g., JWT, HMAC) valid for 15–30 minutes;  
(3) **Token sent via encrypted channel** (e.g., TLS) to the registered email;  
(4) **User accesses token via secure link**—no password or sensitive data is transmitted;  
(5) **System verifies token integrity, expiration, and origin**;  
(6) **User sets new password** on a secure, HTTPS-protected page;  
(7) **New password is hashed and stored** (never plaintext);  
(8) **Old session invalidated**, MFA re-enabled if applicable.  

All steps are logged, encrypted, and auditable. Sensitive data (e.g., old password, token) is never exposed. The process complies with GDPR, FCRA, and NIST SP 800-63B. Unauthorized access is blocked by token expiry, rate limiting, and MFA.

