Consent must be specific, revocable, and documented. Law enforcement access requires judicial oversight. Unauthorized access—by private entities or individuals—violates GDPR, FCRA, and computer misuse laws. Real-time location data remains protected under privacy principles: lawfulness, purpose limitation, and data minimization. No access is lawful without a valid legal basis or explicit user authorization.

