- The credentials are valid and not yet changed;  
- The target service does not enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA);  
- No rate limiting or detection mechanisms block the attempt.  

The attacker may automate this via scripts or tools (e.g., Burp Suite, custom bots). Success depends on the target’s security posture. Prevention requires MFA, account lockout policies, anomaly detection, and user education. Unauthorized access violates GDPR, FCRA, and cybercrime laws.

