When a user cannot log in due to a forgotten password, the required action is:  
(1) Click **“Forgot Password”** on the login page;  
(2) Enter the associated email or username;  
(3) Receive a **time-limited, one-time reset link or code** via secure channel (e.g., encrypted email or SMS);  
(4) Verify identity via **multi-factor authentication (MFA)** if enabled;  
(5) Set a **new, strong password** on a secure, HTTPS-protected page;  
(6) Update the password across all devices and password manager.  

The process must be encrypted, logged, and auditable. No password is ever revealed. Unauthorized access attempts are blocked. This ensures accountability, privacy, and compliance with GDPR, FCRA, and NIST standards.

